# Line endings — one rule for the whole repo (08_ROAD_TO_10.md §1.1).
#
# The tree currently holds a MIX of CRLF and LF: the analytics/calls/crm/tenancy
# controllers are CRLF, almost everything else is LF. That has already cost a
# real debugging cycle — a codemod whose regex was anchored on `";\n` silently
# skipped every CRLF file and reported success. Normalising in the index removes
# the class of bug entirely, and pairs with Prettier's `"endOfLine": "lf"`
# (platform/.prettierrc.json) which keeps new writes consistent.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide text-vs-binary by content; `eol=lf` then pins the
# checked-out ending on every platform, Windows included. Nothing here needs
# CRLF in the working tree: there are no .bat/.cmd files and no gradlew wrapper.
#
# NOTE FOR WHOEVER LANDS THIS: the working tree is not rewritten until someone
# runs `git add --renormalize .` and commits the result. Do that on a quiet
# tree, as its own commit, with no other work in flight — it touches every
# CRLF file and will conflict with anything open.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary — never diffed, never merged, never EOL-converted.
#
# `text=auto` guesses from content and is usually right, but a guess that goes
# wrong on a keystore or an APK corrupts the artifact irrecoverably, so the
# formats we actually produce or carry are declared explicitly. Most of these
# are .gitignore'd today (CallRecorderApp/.gitignore excludes *.jks/*.apk, and
# app/build/ output); the declarations exist so that the day one is force-added
# or an ignore rule is relaxed, it lands intact.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Android build output and release signing material (CallRecorderApp/).
*.apk       binary
*.aab       binary
*.dex       binary
*.aar       binary
*.jar       binary
*.so        binary
*.jks       binary
*.keystore  binary
*.p12       binary
*.bin       binary

# Documents — "Build docs/" carries PDFs alongside the markdown.
*.pdf       binary
*.docx      binary
*.xlsx      binary
*.pptx      binary

# Images and fonts (Android drawables, console assets).
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.webp      binary
*.ico       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
*.eot       binary

# Audio and video. This is a call-recording product: OEM captures and test
# fixtures are exactly the files a stray CRLF conversion would silently ruin.
*.amr       binary
*.3gp       binary
*.m4a       binary
*.aac       binary
*.mp3       binary
*.wav       binary
*.ogg       binary
*.opus      binary
*.flac      binary
*.mp4       binary

# Archives.
*.zip       binary
*.gz        binary
*.tgz       binary
*.bz2       binary
*.xz        binary
*.7z        binary
